509 /* ---- §6.3 document form. Inside a .k-doc the report's panels stop being
510    boxes and become sections: hairline rules and whitespace instead of cards,
511    because a research page that grows boxes reads as a dashboard, and that is
512    where a research surface loses the seriousness it needs to be trusted.
513 
514    The MARKUP is untouched. Every _panel_head() call site, every cross-link
515    target, comment anchor and panel_id keeps working — only presentation
516    changes. That is why this is a scoped stylesheet block and not a rewrite of
517    twenty renderers: the alternative was hand-editing every call site, which
518    would have churned the goldens structurally for a purely visual change.
519 
520    --panel-pad-x is the one lever. Heads, .val-rows, .tbl cells and the strip
521    lists all take their horizontal padding from it, so zeroing it here flushes
522    the whole section to the document's left edge in one declaration. ---- */
523 .k-doc .panel {
524   --panel-pad-x: 0px;
525   border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: none; overflow: visible;
526   border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
527   padding-top: var(--sp-2);
528 }
529 .k-doc .panel:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
530 .k-doc .panel-head { border-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
531 /* The section label: the kit's caption shape in the editorial mark (§2). */
532 .k-doc .panel-title {
533   font-size: var(--fs-caption); font-weight: 600; color: var(--mark);
534   text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.16em;
535 }
536 /* A document's own prose keeps the reading measure even though the report
537    itself is fluid — .k-doc-fluid drops the outer clamp, not this one. */
538 .k-doc .lede { max-width: var(--k-measure); }
539 
540 /* P4.1 canonical header anatomy: title (left) · as-of · source chip · sub
541    (right edge, grouped in .panel-meta). Built by workspace_html._panel_head —
542    hand-rolled heads should not exist outside that helper. */
543 .panel-meta {
544   display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px;
545   min-width: 0; text-align: right;
546 }
547 .panel-asof {
